WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.360
How can an organ change the whole body without its own nerves?

2
00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:10.600
In 1849, a Göttingen physician put a testis back into the belly of castrated young

3
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:16.240
cockerels. Even cut off from its original nerves, that organ let the birds grow

4
00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:17.240
combs and crow.

5
00:00:20.367 --> 00:00:23.707
To find a chemical signal, you first take its source away.

6
00:00:25.087 --> 00:00:29.107
Removing a gland, or disabling it with a lesion, is called extirpation.

7
00:00:30.447 --> 00:00:35.287
Once secretion stops, normal clearance drains the blood level down, and the target

8
00:00:35.287 --> 00:00:40.787
response falls. Removal shows need, yet surgery might also cut nerves.

9
00:00:41.867 --> 00:00:44.947
To rule out cut nerves, you next test replacement.

10
00:00:46.247 --> 00:00:50.347
Place the organ in a new spot, or deliver the missing hormone directly.

11
00:00:51.847 --> 00:00:54.887
Droplets refill the blood, and the target response recovers.

12
00:00:56.287 --> 00:01:00.667
If function returns without original nerves, a chemical carries the signal.

13
00:01:01.767 --> 00:01:07.867
To test blood transport directly, experimenters use parabiosis, joining two animals'

14
00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:13.827
circulations. In joined mice, blood-borne factors cross while each nervous system

15
00:01:13.827 --> 00:01:17.047
stays separate. Here is the core rule.

16
00:01:18.327 --> 00:01:23.387
Remove the source to test need, replace the signal to restore function, and join

17
00:01:23.387 --> 00:01:25.007
bloodstreams to test transport.

18
00:01:26.117 --> 00:01:30.317
Yet replacement is not always as simple as adding hormone back.

19
00:01:31.577 --> 00:01:36.477
In rhesus monkeys, hypothalamic lesions cut off gonadotropin-releasing hormone,

20
00:01:37.097 --> 00:01:43.977
called GnRH. A pump replaces it as hourly bursts, or as a steady drip giving at

21
00:01:43.977 --> 00:01:49.377
least as much. Which schedule restores the pituitary's release of its two

22
00:01:49.377 --> 00:01:50.497
reproductive hormones?

23
00:01:56.150 --> 00:02:01.750
Only the hourly bursts restore luteinizing hormone and follicle-stimulating hormone.

24
00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:05.610
The steady drip shuts pituitary release down.

25
00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:08.170
The drip ran at four rates.

26
00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:12.770
The two highest gave as much hormone as the pulses, or more.

27
00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:15.730
So dose cannot explain the failure.

28
00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:22.990
The usual answer is desensitization: constant hormone makes pituitary cells turn

29
00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:24.070
their response down.

30
00:02:25.167 --> 00:02:28.827
Replacement also fails when a hormone is not missing.

31
00:02:30.227 --> 00:02:33.967
Fat cells make leptin, a fuel gauge reporting stored energy.

32
00:02:35.447 --> 00:02:41.067
Leptin replacement worked in ob/ob mice, which lack leptin, and in rare people

33
00:02:41.067 --> 00:02:42.227
unable to make it.

34
00:02:43.387 --> 00:02:48.487
Most people with common obesity have high leptin, so replacement does not reliably

35
00:02:48.487 --> 00:02:49.487
help.

36
00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:57.110
In 1849, relocating a testis in castrated cockerels showed an organ can act without

37
00:02:57.110 --> 00:03:03.750
original nerves. In rhesus monkeys, pulsed GnRH replacement showed that signal

38
00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:07.330
timing matters. Medicine uses that rule.

39
00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:15.190
Leuprolide, a slow-release GnRH relative, stays steady, so the pituitary quiets and

40
00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:17.490
testosterone falls in prostate cancer.

41
00:03:18.583 --> 00:03:25.123
In 1996, Ahima and colleagues showed falling leptin in fasting mice helps set off

42
00:03:25.123 --> 00:03:26.303
the starvation response.

43
00:03:27.703 --> 00:03:31.423
Because leptin tracks stored energy, its drop signals low fuel.

44
00:03:32.743 --> 00:03:37.323
Take away the source, restore the pattern, and shared blood reveals what steers the

45
00:03:37.323 --> 00:03:37.583
body.
